{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1617 / #EXP-1804, redesigned by #EXP-2172 (the approved CI redesign, session 64abb994, Danny 2026-11-27): THE CI RUN PAGE (view `ci-run`, ×4: web /t/$teamSlug/ci/$runId?job=<jobId>, the desktop, iOS, Android; the target of every check's `details_url` our CI writes). genUI catalog only. DATA: the synced `ci_runs` row (with `title`, `provider`, `externalUrl`, `externalAccess`) + its `ci_jobs` rows, the runner devices' labels, the PR (number, base), the author (users shape), the repository's full name, and the selected job's LOG fetched on demand (tRPC `ci.log{jobId, offset}` → {text, nextOffset, complete}; read once from 0, then while not complete from `nextOffset` every `liveTailMs`; a GitHub job's log comes from GitHub once it finished, reading empty while it runs). THE HEAD (#EXP-2169 \"one look\": no Breadcrumb, as the issue page has none; the sidebar and the work tab navigate): the `Heading` = the run's TITLE (ci-page.json's row title rule) and a muted line `name #n · repository · <age>` (the age = the catalog's formatRelativeTime of startedAt, else createdAt); phones put `name #n` / repository in the platform's page header and start the tree with the title. Then ONE LINE: the CHIP STRIP (`chips`: status with its dot, ref → base, sha, #PR, author, duration, runners; a chip without data is left out) and the ACTIONS (`actions`): THE one default Button = `primary` (copy.cancel = `ci.cancel{runId}` while it runs or waits; copy.rerunFailed = `ci.rerun{runId, failedOnly: true}` after a failure; copy.rerunAll = `ci.rerun{failedOnly: false}` after a pass; then open the returned run when it differs: ours = a new run, GitHub = the same run, a new attempt), copy.fix (outline, icon bot) when it failed = THE new-chat composer on the run's team and repository with `fixPrompt` as its text, and a ⋯ `Menu` (Button ghost icon `ellipsis`, copy.more) of `menu`: copy.rerunAll, copy.openExternal (opens externalUrl). A GitHub run without Actions: write has no primary (Open on GitHub stays in ⋯). Wide: a Toolbar with the chips and the actions in its trailing slot; phones: the chips wrap, the actions below. FAILURE SUMMARY (`failureSummary`): once the selected FAILED job's log is read and holds an error line, an `Alert` type error: title copy.failure.title, message = its first error line; none before (logs are read on demand; no test counting). An `error` run (the pipeline file did not plan) shows an Alert copy.pipelineError with the error instead of the jobs. JOBS (`jobRows` in planner order; statuses and tones = ci-page.json `statusTones`; `jobsCaption` = the non-zero counts failed · running · queued · passed · skipped): WIDE a `Section` titled copy.jobs, caption the counts, one `Row` per job (leading the status Icon, title = check name, subtitle = reason text, meta = duration, selected) beside the selected job's `Card` (title = its check name, description = `jobSummary`: `Failed after {d}` / `Passed in {d}` / `Running for {d}` (+ ` on {runner}`), copy.jobSummary.queued, a skip's reason) holding its steps as a `Trace` of collapsible `TraceItem`s (title, status, description = duration) where the failed (else running, else last) step is OPEN and holds the log: ONE `CodeBlock{title: copy.log, language: ansi, lineNumbers: true, wrap: false, copyable: true, maxLines: logMaxLines.wide | .phone, highlight: logView(text).highlight, follow: the job is not completed}` (copy.emptyLog as muted Text when the job has no log and is not running; a job without steps shows the log under the card's head). PHONES the Section rows carry a chevron and DRILL into the job (`jobOpen`): the job's Card alone (the platform's back returns). A JobGraph of stages comes with genUI (#EXP-2204). SELECTION (`defaultJob`): the `job` query param when it names a job of the run, else the first FAILING job, else the first RUNNING one, else the first; selecting rewrites `?job=`. `steps`: queued → pending, in_progress → running, completed success → done, skipped/neutral → skipped, other → error; description = its duration. `logView`: `##[group]X` → `▸ X`, `##[endgroup]` dropped, `##[error]X` → `Error: X` (its displayed line into `highlight`), `##[warning]X` → `Warning: X`; a trailing newline adds no empty last line. `fixPrompt`: copy.fixPrompt.head (sha = its 7), .job when a failing job is named, .read, then, when the log is read, a blank line, .tail and the last `fixLogLines` lines of logView(log).code in a ```text fence. testIds name the parts for the e2e/shots. The trees are pinned by ci-run-view.json.",
